From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:09:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/30] drm/panel: jadard: add the Teclast P25T panel (JD9365)

The Teclast P25T (P9A6, RK3566) has an 800x1280 JD9365 MIPI-DSI panel
on four lanes. Add its init sequence (202 commands, converted from the
stock device tree), its mode (67 MHz, 135 x 216 mm) and the compatible
"teclast,p25t-panel".

Two things differ from the other JD9365 panels in this driver, both
needed on this board:
- The init sequence is sent in high-speed mode (no MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM)
  with a non-continuous clock lane, as on the Anbernic RG-DS (RK3568 +
  JD9365).
- No DCS reads after the init: on this board a read never gets an
  answer and leaves data lane 0 turned around, which stops the video
  stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019kgfNtsGWnCDNQnFvegC9W
